# ==============================================================================
# MDI TMLE: ANALYSIS USING PARAMETRIC GLM and SUPERLEARNER +/- truncation 
# ==============================================================================
#
# INPUT:
#   example: mdi_lmtp_wide_3month.csv
#
# RUNS:
#   1. Parametric GLM     + truncation
#   2. Parametric GLM     + no truncation
#   3. Super Learner      + truncation
#   4. Super Learner      + no truncation
#
# Super Learner library:
#   SL.mean
#   SL.glm
#   SL.ranger
#   SL.rpart
#   SL.glmnet.ridge
#
# Primary analysis = Parametric GLM, truncation at 99.9th percentile, 3-monthly time discretisation, cross-fitting 5-folds 
#
# Variations studied: 
#   1. Nuisance function estimation (parametric GLM, ensemble super learner)
#   2. Truncation of weights 
#   3. Cross-fitting folds
# 
# CV:
#   outer LMTP/TMLE cross-fitting = 5
#   nuisance-function SuperLearner CV = 5
#
# SAVED FOR EVERY RUN:
#   - full EMPA fit
#   - full DPP-4i fit
#   - effect result
#   - survival/risk result
#   - outcome regression matrices
#   - full nuisance fits / SL fits
#   - non-cumulative density ratios at every time point
#   - cumulative density-ratio weights at every time point
#   - matched density ratios for the observed treatment arm
#   - DR1 individual values
#   - DR1 top 100
#   - DR1 summary
#   - density-ratio summaries for all time points
#   - DR1 histogram and density plot
#   - runtime
#   - session information
#
# FINAL:
#   one 4-row summary table
# ==============================================================================

